# Commits that git blame skips: generated moves and scripted rewrites that
# change where code lives or what it is called, not what it does.
#
# The refactor plan (docs/plans/codebase-refactor.md §6.9) lists here the
# merged commit of every class A pure move and class R scripted rewrite.
# After such a pull request merges, a class T follow-up adds that commit's
# full SHA, one per line with a comment naming the step. A move regenerated
# before it merged has a new SHA, so only the one that merged is listed. A
# squash merge lists the squashed commit.
#
# GitHub's blame view reads this file on its own. Locally, turn it on once
# per clone:
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# or for one run: git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs <file>.
# `git log --follow` still shows every commit.
